  a skos:Concept ;
  skos:prefLabel "Contingency Provision/ Reserves"@en ;
  schema:category Income and Expenditure|Operating Costs|Other|Contingency Provision/ Reserves ;
  skos:definition A financial reserve established to sustain operations for up to 12 months in the event of an orderly wind-down. Classified under operating costs, this contingency fund is maintained separately from reserves covering operational risk or development investment, and represents a high-priority allocation within an organization's expenditure planning. ;
