  schema:category Trust|Certification|Software Development Quality|List of Certifications: Software Quality|Software Quality End Date ;
  skos:definition Software Quality End Date denotes the date on which a software quality certification expires or ceases to be valid. It marks the temporal boundary of a certification's validity period, after which the certification is no longer considered current or authoritative. ;
